# kex: check-only
# A reserved word naming a plain `let` BINDING, not a make-block method.
#
# `error_reserved_keyword_name.kex` covers the make-block spelling. This one is
# the value binding: neither the let-function-definition lookahead nor the
# pattern parser can claim a keyword, so `let compiled = ...` fell through to a
# bare "Expected pattern" that named neither the word nor the problem — and
# then, because recovery resumes on exactly the tokens that report a
# declaration, the parser landed straight back on `compiled` and added a second
# meaningless "Expected 'do' after 'compiled', got =".
#
# Found while porting Rodolfo (docs/rodolfo-findings.md).
let compiled = 1

main do
  IO.printLine("unreachable")
end
